  "title": "Time, seasons and weather",
  "note": "Months are adjectives agreeing with mensis (m): mensis Martius, March. Dates count back from three fixed days: Kalendae (the 1st), Nonae (the 5th, or 7th in March, May, July and October) and Idus (the 13th, or 15th in those months). Time when uses the ablative without a preposition: hieme, in winter. Weather verbs have no subject: pluit, it rains.",
